<title>POLAND: ESPEBEPE DROPS AS ECONOMIC WOES GO ON.</title>
<headline>ESPEBEPE DROPS AS ECONOMIC WOES GO ON.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction firm Espebepe SA fell 8.8 percent to 3.1 zlotys in light trade on Monday's news the firm's financial woes had continued in October, analysts said.</p>
<p>Espebepe made a net loss of 3.1 million zlotys in October and 19.6 million zlotys over the first 10 months this year.</p>
<p>&quot;The firm's poor economic situation is reflected in its share price,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The company said last month it could go bankrupt if its creditors did not agree to a debt-write-off deal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
